---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Delta and United Airline Statistical Analysis"
  category="Data Analysis · Statistics · Airline Operations"
  status="Completed"
  summary="A MATLAB-based analysis of 2015–2024 Bureau of Transportation Statistics data investigating whether fuel cost, operational scale, passenger demand, and seasonal variation could help explain profitability differences between Delta and United."
  tools={["MATLAB", "BTS Data", "Statistical Testing"]}
>
  <div class="case-study-page">
    <section class="case-study-card context-card">
      <div class="context-icon-slot" aria-label="Left context icon placeholder"><span>ICON</span></div>

      <div class="context-copy">
        <h2>Project Context</h2>
        <p>
          This project investigated why Delta Airlines showed greater average profitability than United Airlines despite operating under similar fuel-use conditions. I evaluated whether fuel price, flight volume, passenger demand, and seasonal variation could help explain the difference while identifying the limits of the available data.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="context-icon-slot" aria-label="Right context icon placeholder"><span>ICON</span></div>
    </section>
    <section class="case-study-card split-card">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <h2>Dataset and Variables</h2>
        <p>
          I organized quarterly and yearly Bureau of Transportation Statistics data covering 2015 through 2024. The variables included fuel cost per gallon, total fuel consumed, total fuel cost, load factor, number of flights, net income, revenue passenger miles, and operating revenue.
        </p>
        <p>
          The dataset was structured so the two airlines could be compared consistently across time while preserving the quarterly relationships needed for hypothesis testing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="carousel" data-carousel>
        <div class="carousel-frame">
          <div class="carousel-slide is-active" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Dataset / descriptive chart 1</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Dataset / descriptive chart 2</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Dataset / descriptive chart 3</div>
          </div>

          <button class="carousel-arrow previous" type="button" data-previous aria-label="Previous dataset visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
          <button class="carousel-arrow next" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next dataset visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel-dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="is-active" data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="case-study-card split-card reverse-card">
      <div class="carousel" data-carousel>
        <div class="carousel-frame">
          <div class="carousel-slide is-active" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Statistical test visual 1</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Regression visual 2</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Seasonality visual 3</div>
          </div>

          <button class="carousel-arrow previous" type="button" data-previous aria-label="Previous statistical analysis visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
          <button class="carousel-arrow next" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next statistical analysis visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel-dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="is-active" data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-copy">
        <h2>Statistical Analysis Approach</h2>
        <p>
          I cleaned and separated the airline data, calculated descriptive statistics, and evaluated the assumptions required for each statistical test. Because the observations were measured over time, I used first-differencing where appropriate to reduce dependence between consecutive values.
        </p>
        <p>
          I used a paired t-test for quarterly fuel-cost changes, a robust multiple-regression model for changes in net income, and a Kruskal–Wallis test to evaluate seasonal variation in Delta revenue passenger miles per flight.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="case-study-card split-card">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <h2>Results and Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          The paired fuel-cost test produced a p-value of 0.6092. None of the multiple-regression predictors reached statistical significance at α = 0.05, with flight volume producing the smallest predictor p-value at approximately 0.0958. The seasonal Kruskal–Wallis test produced a p-value of 0.2026.
        </p>
        <p>
          The descriptive results suggested that operational scale was a more promising explanation than fuel pricing, but the tests did not prove that it caused the profitability difference. Remaining autocorrelation, small seasonal groups, and missing route- and aircraft-specific variables limited the strength of the conclusions.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="carousel" data-carousel>
        <div class="carousel-frame">
          <div class="carousel-slide is-active" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Key results chart 1</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Key results chart 2</div>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-slide" data-slide>
            <div class="carousel-placeholder">Limitations / residual visual 3</div>
          </div>

          <button class="carousel-arrow previous" type="button" data-previous aria-label="Previous results visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 5l-7 7 7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
          <button class="carousel-arrow next" type="button" data-next aria-label="Next results visualization">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="carousel-dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="is-active" data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
          <span data-dot></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="overall-section">
      <div class="overall-heading">
        <span></span>
        <h2>Overall</h2>
        <span></span>
      </div>

      <div class="overall-grid">
        <article class="overall-card">
          <h3>Results</h3>
          <p>The analysis found no statistically significant difference in quarterly fuel-price changes and did not establish a significant seasonal effect or statistically significant regression predictor at α = 0.05.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="overall-card">
          <h3>My Contributions</h3>
          <p>I organized and cleaned the BTS data in MATLAB, selected and implemented the statistical tests, evaluated model assumptions, and interpreted the results without overstating what the models proved.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="overall-card">
          <h3>Lessons Learned</h3>
          <p>The project strengthened my ability to work with real-world datasets, check statistical assumptions, and communicate uncertainty when observed patterns are not strongly supported by hypothesis tests.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</ProjectLayout>


<style>
  .case-study-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 30px;
  }

  .case-study-card {
    border: 1px solid #bfd2e5;
    border-radius: 18px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.72);
  }

  .context-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 150px minmax(0, 760px) 150px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 46px;
    min-height: 270px;
    padding: 46px 54px;
  }

  .context-copy {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .context-copy h2,
  .section-copy h2,
  .overall-heading h2,
  .overall-card h3 {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .context-copy h2 {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .context-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: justify;
    text-align-last: center;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .context-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 18px;
  }

  .context-icon-slot {
    display: grid;
    width: 94px;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    place-items: center;
    justify-self: center;
    border: 2px dashed #78aee8;
    border-radius: 14px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 850;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }

  .split-card {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.88fr) minmax(0, 1.12fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 54px;
    padding: 28px 34px;
  }

  .reverse-card {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.12fr) minmax(0, 0.88fr);
  }

  .section-copy {
    padding: 18px 14px;
  }

  .section-copy h2 {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 2.7vw, 2.7rem);
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .section-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 1.06rem;
  }

  .section-copy p + p {
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .carousel {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .carousel-frame {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: 7px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 17px;
    background: #eaf1f8;
  }

  .carousel-slide {
    display: none;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  .carousel-slide.is-active {
    display: block;
  }

  .carousel-slide img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: contain;
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .carousel-placeholder {
    display: grid;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    place-items: center;
    padding: 24px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(20, 126, 223, 0.035), rgba(20, 126, 223, 0.09)),
      #eef4fa;
    color: #6f8297;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .carousel-arrow {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    display: grid;
    width: 48px;
    height: 48px;
    place-items: center;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid #d5e0ea;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.94);
    color: var(--accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    box-shadow: 0 3px 12px rgba(18, 32, 58, 0.12);
  }

  .carousel-arrow:hover {
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .carousel-arrow svg {
    width: 25px;
    height: 25px;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .carousel-arrow.previous {
    left: 14px;
  }

  .carousel-arrow.next {
    right: 14px;
  }

  .carousel-dots {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 13px;
  }

  .carousel-dots span {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #cbd6e1;
  }

  .carousel-dots span.is-active {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .overall-section {
    padding-top: 4px;
  }

  .overall-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .overall-heading span {
    height: 2px;
    background: #a9c9e8;
  }

  .overall-heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 2.6vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .overall-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 22px;
  }

  .overall-card {
    min-height: 190px;
    padding: 28px 30px;
    border: 1px solid #91bae2;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.76);
  }

  .overall-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 13px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .overall-card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .context-card {
      grid-template-columns: 90px minmax(0, 1fr) 90px;
      gap: 26px;
      padding: 38px 30px;
    }

    .split-card,
    .reverse-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .reverse-card .carousel {
      order: 2;
    }

    .reverse-card .section-copy {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .case-study-page {
      gap: 20px;
    }

    .context-card {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 20px;
      min-height: 0;
      padding: 30px 24px;
    }

    .context-icon-slot {
      display: none;
    }

    .context-copy p {
      text-align: left;
      text-align-last: auto;
    }

    .split-card,
    .reverse-card {
      padding: 20px;
    }

    .section-copy {
      padding: 6px 2px;
    }

    .section-copy h2 {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .carousel-frame {
      border-width: 5px;
    }

    .carousel-arrow {
      width: 42px;
      height: 42px;
    }

    .overall-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>


<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-carousel]").forEach((carousel) => {
    const slides = Array.from(carousel.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-slide]"));
    const dots = Array.from(carousel.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-dot]"));
    const previous = carousel.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-previous]");
    const next = carousel.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-next]");

    let activeIndex = 0;

    const showSlide = (index: number) => {
      activeIndex = (index + slides.length) % slides.length;

      slides.forEach((slide, slideIndex) => {
        const active = slideIndex === activeIndex;
        slide.classList.toggle("is-active", active);
        slide.setAttribute("aria-hidden", String(!active));
      });

      dots.forEach((dot, dotIndex) => {
        dot.classList.toggle("is-active", dotIndex === activeIndex);
      });
    };

    previous?.addEventListener("click", () => showSlide(activeIndex - 1));
    next?.addEventListener("click", () => showSlide(activeIndex + 1));

    showSlide(0);
  });
</script>
